    "### **Feature Extraction Methods**  \n",
    "We experimented with three different ways of transforming text into numerical features:\n",
    "1. **Bag of Words (BoW)** – Representing text as a frequency-based vector. We tested BoW with 2 different n-gram ranges:\n",
    "   - Unigrams (1-gram) without stopwords\n",
    "   - Bigrams (2-grams) with stopwords\n",
    "2. **Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency (TF-IDF)** – Adjusting word importance based on frequency in documents (samples).\n",
    "3. **Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) with 200 components** – A dimensionality reduction technique applied to BoW and TF-IDF.\n",
    "4. **Word Embeddings (Word2Vec)** – Dense vector representations of words.\n",
    "\n",
    "### **Model Types**  \n",
    "We evaluated three machine learning classifiers:\n",
    "1. **Support Vector Machine (SVM)** – A strong baseline for text classification, known for its high accuracy but often slow training.\n",
    "2. **Naïve Bayes (NB)** – A probabilistic classifier that is fast and interpretable.\n",
    "3. **Logistic Regression (LR)** – A model that performs linear mapping of features to classes, often used for binary classification but can be extended to multi-class problems.\n",
    "\n",
    "### **Hyperparameter Variations**  \n",
    "- **Naïve Bayes (NB)** was tested with different smoothing parameters (`alpha` values).  \n",
    "- **Logistic Regression (LR)** used different combinations of:\n",
    "  - `C` (regularization strength),\n",
    "  - `penalty` (`l1` or `l2`),\n",
    "  - `solver` (`liblinear`, `saga`)\n",
    "- **Support Vector Machine (SVM)** was tested with different kernel types (`linear`, `rbf`, `sigmoid`), regularization parameters (`C`) and gamma values (`scale`, `auto`).\n",
    "\n",
    "### **Additional Parameter: include_digits**  \n",
    "We conducted experiments with and without digit inclusion in text processing. The goal is to assess the impact of digits inclusion on model performance. Are they relevant for politeness classification?\n",
    "\n",
    "## **Validation pipeline**\n",
    "The validation process aims to find the preprocessing configuration and model that yields the best performance  (accuracy) on the validation set. The best configuration is then used to evaluate the model on the test set, providing an unbiased estimate of its performance on unseen data."
   ]
  },
